# selinux

- logging
ausearch -m avc -ts recent
(pipe to less and search for name to find patterns)

- list dontaudit rules
sesearch -D (from setools-console pkg)

common issues:
1. nonstandard locations for service data
- add context type to dir recursively
semanage fcontext -a -t httpd_sys_content_t '/mysites/sitea/www(/.*)?'
restorecon -Rv /mysites/sitea/www

2. swithching from disabled to enforcing
touch /.autorelabel
reboot

3. wrong booleans (setroubleshoot-server pkg)
semanage boolean list
getsebool
setsebool

4. nonstandard ports
semanage port -a -t http_port_t -p tcp 8001 # if conflicts with existing label, add policy module

understanding selinux rules  (setools-console pkg)
- info on type
seinfo -thttpd_sys_content_t
- info on port
seinfo --portcon=443 --protocol=tcp
- info on what boolean allows
sesearch --allow -b httpd_can_connect_ldap

# pam - authentication for apps and services
- configs per service in /etc/pam.d/, format:
type control module-path [module args]
- type is one of account, auth, password, and session
- control: required, requisite, sufficient, optional, include, or substack
- module-path: absolute or relative to /lib/security/ or /lib64/security/
authconfig --updateall # erase manual changes

# kerberos
cat /etc/krb5.conf
- possible issues:
default_realm setting wrong, perms on keytab (klist -ek <file> to inspect), DNS SRV records for Kerberos incorect (if used), check krb5_realm and krb5_server settings in /etc/sssd/sssd.conf, issues in nfs shares

# LDAP (openldap-clients pkg)
/etc/openldap/ldap.conf
ldapsearch -x
ldapsearch -x -ZZ
ldapsearch -x -ZZ -LL '(uid=ldapuser)' cn homeDirectory # search for ldap servers
/etc/openldap/cacerts  # check in case of tls errors
- if loading certs there:
wget -O /etc/openldap/cacerts/example-ca.crt ftp://<src>/pub/example-ca.crt
cacertdir_rehash /etc/openldap/cacerts
-- restart sshd and autofs services

